 "answer": "The latest reading I found puts Shah Alam's API at **180, which is in the \"Unhealthy\" range**. That figure was taken at **5pm today (16 October)**. It comes from the Malaysian Air Pollutant Index Management System (APIMS), as reported by Focus Malaysia.\n\n**Elsewhere in Selangor at the same time:**\n- Klang: 195, the highest in Malaysia\n- Johan Setia: 192\n- Banting: 174\n- Petaling Jaya: 169\n- Kuala Selangor: 161\n\nAcross the country, 34 places had unhealthy readings, and none had good air quality.\n\n**What the numbers mean:**\n- 0–50: Good\n- 51–100: Moderate\n- 101–200: Unhealthy\n- 201–300: Very unhealthy\n- Over 300: Hazardous\n\n**Health tip:** At this level, try to spend less time outdoors. This matters most for children, older people, and anyone with asthma or heart or lung problems. If you need to go out, wear an N95 mask.\n\nThe API is updated every hour, so the number may have changed since 5pm. For the current reading, check the APIMS website (eqms.doe.gov.my) or the MyIPU app.",
